      "message": "In this scenario, `pd_get_partner_rmdo` and `pd_dpm_request` would still run when the port is disconnected. Or am I missing something in your suggestion?\n\nIf `pd_send_alert_msg` were changed to return `EC_SUCCESS` at the top when the port is not connected, the check in `pd_broadcast_alert_msg` could be removed, but returning success when the port is not connected seems wrong.",
